## Requirements

| Component | Minimum | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| OS | Linux, macOS, Windows 11 (WSL2) | any platform with a supported runtime |
| Runtime | Python 3.10 or Node.js 20 | whichever this project ships with |
| Git | 2.40 | needed for the clone and push steps |
| Docker (optional) | 24 | only for the container workflow |

## Installation

Check [Requirements](#requirements) first, then copy the lines that match your project.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{FULL_NAME}}.git
cd {{REPO}} && git switch {{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}

uv sync                   # install dependencies (Node.js projects: pnpm install)
```

## Quick start

The options are documented in [Configuration](#configuration).

```bash
cp config.example.yml config.yml          # 1. start from the sample configuration
$EDITOR config.yml                        # 2. replace the placeholders; never commit secrets
{{REPO}} --config config.yml --dry-run    # 3. preview — nothing is written yet
{{REPO}} --config config.yml              # 4. run for real ({{REPO}} = this project's entry point)
```

## Usage

Run `{{REPO}} --help` for the full flag list; the settings most people touch are in [Configuration](#configuration).

## Configuration

| Option | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `--config` | path | `config.yml` | configuration file to read |
| `--dry-run` | flag | `false` | print the planned actions and write nothing |
| `--api-key` | string | `$API_KEY` | API credential (`<YOUR_API_KEY>`); prefer the environment variable |
| `--verbose` | flag | `false` | more log output, handy in a bug report |

> **Note**: values such as `<YOUR_API_KEY>`, `you@example.com`, `192.0.2.10` and `Example Corp`
> are **placeholders** — replace them before you run anything. Keep real credentials in
> environment variables or a local, uncommitted `.env`; see [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).

## FAQ

**The sample command fails with an authentication error.** You are still using a placeholder
credential — create a real one locally, pass it through an environment variable. See [Configuration](#configuration).

**Should I edit both READMEs?** Yes: change `README.md` first, then mirror the edit into
`README.zh-CN.md`. Section order, badges, commands and image paths stay identical.

**How do I report a security problem?** Not in a public issue — follow [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md)
and write to {{EMAIL}}.

